      "Grade 8 · Reading and viewing: reads a speech, identifying and discussing the key features, analysing language use, emotive or manipulative language and the introduction and conclusion, and reads for comprehension, identifying purpose and target group, manipulative language, how language and images reflect and shape values and attitudes and the impact of font types and sizes, headings and captions on meaning",
      "Grade 8 · Reading and viewing: reads poetry, studying the key features of a poem including the internal structure with figures of speech and imagery, rhyme and rhythm, the external structure of lines, stanzas and typography, figurative meaning, mood and theme and message, and reads a recorded television, radio or simulation forum",
      "Grade 8 · Reading and viewing: reads an information text with visuals such as maps, landmarks and scales, studying the format, language use and features, and reads written or visual texts such as cartoons and comic strips for comprehension, making inferences, inferring the meaning of unfamiliar words by word attack skills and identifying emotive language",
      "Grade 8 · Reading and viewing: reads a literary text such as drama, a play or a one-act play, explaining plot, sub-plot, character portrayal, conflict and dramatic response and identifying themes, mood and tone, and applies reading strategies for comprehension including purpose and target group, making inferences, giving own opinion, distinguishing fact from opinion and direct and implied meaning",
      "Grade 8 · Reading and viewing: reads a newspaper or magazine article about current or social issues, studying the format, text features, language use, tone and sequencing, and reads a dialogue for comprehension, considering theme and message, inferences, own opinion, direct and implied meaning and the socio-political and cultural background of the text and author",
      "Grade 8 · Reading and viewing: reads written, visual or multimedia texts for information using intensive reading, making inferences, predicting, visualisation, meaning of words and fact and opinion, and prepares for the examination by revising reading comprehension, summaries and literature including the novel, short stories, folklore, drama and film study and poems",
